e contract restricts an operation by authentication or permission, callers lacking that requirement cannot perform it and receive the contract-defined denial response.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-2\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Application state handled by the API is persisted in PostgreSQL through the existing App connection string.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: A successful create or update through the API is written to the PostgreSQL database reached through the App connection string and can be read back by subsequent API requests.\",\n     \"1: A successful delete through the API removes the corresponding persisted data so subsequent reads reflect the deletion, as applicable to the contract operation.\",\n     \"2: When PostgreSQL is unavailable or the configured connection cannot be used, a persistence-dependent operation does not claim success without saving its result.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-3\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"SeedData.Run supplies illustrative demo records for the contract's tables, using contract example values where available; it is sample data, not required production data.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: When Seed:Demo is true and seed data is run, a few believable example rows for each contract table are written to PostgreSQL so contract list operations can return sample records.\",\n     \"1: When Seed:Demo is false or absent, startup does not write the demo rows from SeedData.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-4\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Tests must be valid with demo seeding disabled and must not require the sample records or their specific contents.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: The test suite passes without setting Seed:Demo to true and without relying on demo row counts, identifiers, or field values.\",\n     \"1: Tests that exercise data operations arrange their own required data or otherwise handle an empty database, rather than failing because SeedData did not run.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-5\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"This change delivers the API only; Swagger/OpenAPI tooling is not a product screen and remains distinct from a web application UI.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: The app exposes the API operations and does not add feedlot product screens or UI routes; the web app remains the responsibility of its separate repository.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"sketch\": 2,\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-1\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Treat contracts/openapi.yaml as the complete source of truth: implement its defined API operations and documented request/response behavior, rather than adding operations inferred only from the broader hackathon description.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: For every operation in the locked OpenAPI contract, a request matching its documented method, path, parameters, headers, and body is handled and returns the documented status and response shape.\",\n     \"1: Each operation applies the contract's documented validation and returns its documented error status and response for invalid or missing inputs; it does not silently treat invalid requests as successful.\",\n     \"2: Requests to paths or methods that are not defined by the contract do not act as undocumented contract operations.\",\n     \"3: The documented sign-in operation, POST /auth/sign-in, is available and responds according to its contract definition.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-2\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Persist application data in the existing PostgreSQL database configured by the App connection string; PostgreSQL is the system of record, not an in-memory substitute.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Contract operations that create or update application data write it to the PostgreSQL database configured by App, and subsequent reads return the persisted values.\",\n     \"1: Persisted application data remains available after the API process restarts.\",\n     \"2: When the database cannot be